 inment\, treats\, and a little bit of Halloween weirdness.\nOn Friday\, Oc
 tober 23 from 6-8 PM\, Ashton Avenue will transform into a colorful neighb
 orhood carnival with classic midway games\, prizes\, a bounce house\, obst
 acle course\, face painting\, roaming performers\, music\, and more. Expec
 t a playful mix of vintage circus\, curiosities\, and Halloween fun\; fest
 ive rather than scary\, and designed for kids and grown-ups alike.\n\nCome
  wander the carnival\, try your luck at the games\, catch a performer\, ge
 t your face painted\, and spend an evening with neighbors on Ocean Avenue.
  Costumes are encouraged but absolutely not required.\nCarnival of Curiosi
 ties is free and open to everyone.\nAshton Avenue near Ocean Avenue\, San 
 Francisco\nFriday\, October 23\, 2026\n6:00–8:00 PM\n️ Free admission\
 nPresented by the Ocean Avenue Association with support from the Civic Joy
