BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nureyev
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T210000
DTSTAMP:20261024T111224Z
UID:dothebay-17882102@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Dance
DESCRIPTION:The extraordinary story of an artist who not only transformed 
 the world of ballet\, but stood as a symbol of artistic freedom and indivi
 dual self-determination.\n\nExperience a live performance capture of the m
 ulti-award-winning ballet Nureyev\, choreographed by Yuri Possokhov (San F
 rancisco Ballet Choreographer in Residence) in collaboration with stage di
 rector Kirill Serebrennikov\, with a score by composer Ilya Demutsky.\n\nT
 he production blends ballet\, opera\, and drama into a sweeping homage to 
 one of the 20th century’s greatest dancers\, tracing his rise in the Sov
 iet Union\, his dramatic defection to the West\, his open expression of hi
 s homosexuality\, and his enduring influence on Western ballet.\n\nThe bal
 let premiered at Russia’s Bolshoi Theatre in 2017 to widespread acclaim\
 , but was permanently removed from its repertoire in 2022 under Russia’s
  expanded “gay propaganda” law. Staged by Staatsballett Berlin in 2026
 \, marking the first time Nureyev had been performed outside of Russia\, t
 his live performance capture brings that landmark production to the screen
 .\n\nFollowing the screening\, join Nureyev composer Ilya Demutsky and co-
 stager Dana Genshaft for a live Q&A moderated by SFDFF Artistic Director G
 aren Scribner.\n\nVIP ticket holders are invited to attend a photo opportu
 nity and chat with the creative team immediately after the screening.\n\n3
 0-125\n2026 SF Dance Film Festival:\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/event
 s/2026/10/23/nureyev-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34610964/3fe0e514-e52c-4b74-b65d-3d588dfbbb79.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261024T111224Z
LOCATION:Lucasfilm Premier Theater\, 1110 Gorgas Ave\, San Francisco\, CA\
 , 94129
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/23/nureyev-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Invisible Atlas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T203000
DTSTAMP:20261018T205153Z
UID:funcheap-1641878@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerInvisible Atlas — From Hiros
 hima and Nagasaki to Fukushima: The Invisible Threat of Nuclear Contaminat
 ion\nOctober 23–25\, 2026 | Dance Mission Theater\, San Francisco\nInvis
 ible Atlas\, is a powerful multimedia dance performance exploring the invi
 sible dangers of nuclear contamination and their lasting impact on humanit
 y and the environment.\n\nInspired by the atomic bombings of Hiroshima and
  Nagasaki\, the Fukushima nuclear meltdown\, and ongoing concerns about ra
 dioactive waste in the San Francisco Bay Area\, this performance connects 
 historical tragedies with environmental challenges we face today.\nCombini
 ng Butoh\, contemporary dance\, poetry\, theatrical performance\, immersiv
 e film projections\, and live Japanese Shakuhachi and Taiko music\, Invisi
 ble Atlas creates an emotionally compelling theatrical experience.\nThroug
 h movement\, sound\, and visual storytelling\, the performance invites aud
 iences to reflect on the invisible consequences of nuclear history\, our s
 hared responsibility\, and the future we want to create.\nEvent Informatio
 n\nPerformance Dates & Times:\n\nFriday\, October 23\, 2026 — 7:30 PM\nS
 aturday\, October 24\, 2026 — 7:30 PM\nSunday\, October 25\, 2026 — 4:
 00 PM\n\nVenue: Dance Mission Theater\n3316 24th Street\, San Francisco\, 
 CA 94110\nDirector / Choreographer: Ranko Ogura\nPresented by: Ranko Ogura
  Dance\nDuration: Approximately 60 minutes\nSpecial Ticket Offer: Limited 
 artist & Student tickets available for $20.\nTickets: Available through Hu
 manitix. Plea...\n\n$35.00\n\nTickets: https://invisibleatlas.my.canva.sit
 e\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/invisible-atlas/\nSource: Funcheap SF
LAST-MODIFIED:20261018T205153Z
LOCATION:Dance Mission Theater\, 3316 24th St.\, San Francisco\, CA 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/invisible-atlas/
END:VEVENT
