SUMMARY:“The Great Elephant Migration” 27 Elephant Sculptures Take Ove
 r Livermore (Oct. 10 – Dec. 6)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T210000
DTSTAMP:20261021T000148Z
UID:funcheap-1643570@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:“The Great Elephant Migration” 27 Elephant Sculptures Take
  Over Livermor (Oct. 10 – Dec. 6)\nThree Thirty-Three Arts\nThe Great El
 ephant Migration: A Family Gathering opens in Downtown Livermore with a we
 lcome and blessing ceremony at Stockmen’s Park\, including a cultural da
 nce performance and custom textile artwork. The installation features 30 l
 ife-size handcrafted elephant sculptures by Indigenous artisans at Bankhea
 d Plaza and Stockmen’s Park from October 10 through December 6. Opening-
 day programming also includes the Livermore ArtWalk and an evening Dandiya
  celebration among the elephant sculptures.\nDOWNTOWN LIVERMORE\, CA • O
 CT 10 – DEC 06\, 2026\n27 elephants from The Great Elephant Migration ar
 e visiting the Bay Area for the first time. Greet them on their journey as
  they travel the world sharing a message of coexistence.\nThree Thirty-Thr
 ee Arts and Livermore Valley Arts proudly present The Great Elephant Migra
 tion: A Family Gathering – a two-month public art exhibition featuring 2
 7 life-size sculptures of Indian elephants made from dried lantana plants.
 \nFrom Saturday\, October 10th through Sunday\, December 6th\, The Great E
 lephant Migration: A Family Gathering can be experienced in beautiful Down
 town Livermore. The exhibit is free and accessible to all.\n\n“Bringing 
 the Great Elephant Migration to California gives our communities a unique 
 opportunity to experience art while connecting with a global message of co
 nservation and coexistence\,” said Assemblymember Bauer-Kahan. “I...\n
 \nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.333arts.org/gem\nDetails: https://sf.funche
 ap.com/the-great-elephant-migration-27-elephant-sculptures-take-over-liver
 mor-oct-10-dec-6/\nSource: Funcheap SF
