CATEGORIES:Dance
DESCRIPTION:Vin EiamvuthikornJoin Oceánica Ballet for family-friendly sto
 ry ballets inspired by halloween and Día de los Muertos!\nViva La Vida wi
 th Excerpts from P1N0CCH10 & Carmilla features new works and a returning O
 ceánica Ballet autumn tradition. Act 1 premieres selections from two upco
 ming story ballets. P1N0CCH10\, a retelling of Carlo Collodi’s classic t
 ale\, explores humanity\, artificial intelligence\, and our relationship w
 ith the natural world. Carmilla\, an adaptation of Sheridan Le Fanu’s gr
 oundbreaking sapphic vampire novella\, stages a mysterious masquerade ball
 .\nAct Two features the return of Viva La Vida\, the original story of Luc
 io and Lupita in a joyful folklórico-infused tale about transcending loss
  and the resilience of love\, inspired by Día de los Muertos. In this “
 celebration of life\, loved ones and culture\,” writes Jocelyn Tong of t
 he Daily Californian\, “mythic creatures from the land of the dead … [
 lead to] twirled scarves and snapped-open fans …in a story of homecoming
 .” Throughout all three stories\, the wisdom of women across time and cu
 ltures is amplified.\nViva La Vida with Excerpts from P1N0CCH10 & Carmilla
 \nSunday\, November 1\, 2026 | 1p & 4p\nCollege of San Mateo Theatre\, 170
 0 W Hillsdale Blvd\, San Mateo – Map & Directions\nGet Tickets: Starting
  at $19 ($10 off) – General Admission (fees included)\n\nLimited time of
 fer Lucky 13: 13% off 4:00 performance on Sunday\, November 1st tix when p
 urchased Oct 2 thru Oct 13 2026 while supplies last. Lowest price tickets 
 are $25....\n\n$19.00\n\nTickets: https://oceanicaballet.org/\nDetails: ht
 tps://sf.funcheap.com/ocenica-ballet-2026-san-mateo/\nSource: Funcheap SF
