SUMMARY:Too Much
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T213000
DTSTAMP:20261026T203423Z
UID:dothebay-17997417@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:MOViES FOR MANiACS presents “Get Off the Internet” Film Fe
 stival hosted by Jesse Hawthorne Ficks\n\nWEDNESDAY\, November 04\n\n7:30p
 m TOO MUCH (Cannon Films\, 1987) in 35mm!\n\nThis offbeat\, neo-sincere\, 
 rarely seen 1980s children’s flick follows a young girl (Bridgette Ander
 son of SAVANNAH SMiLES) who while visiting Japan\, falls in love with her 
 new robot named TM.\n\nNever released on home media in the U.S. and unavai
 lable on official streaming site\, this fascinatingly prophetic and surpri
 singly heartwarming Golan/Globus produced gem is the perfect blend of E.T.
  (1982) + SHORT CiRCUiT (1986) + MAC & ME (1985). It’s also an extraordi
 nary time-capsule of Japanese culture in the late 1980s\, made-up by a cas
 t and crew almost entirely from Japan.\n\nRated PG w/ a running time of 89
  minutes. Extremely Rare Original 35mm print. Theatrical screening rights 
 cleared through Park Circus.\n\nThe evening will be preceded by a raffle\,
  trivia and a gaggle of maniacal 35mm trailers.\n\nTickets: https://ticket
 ing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/20307?siteToken=52wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\n
 Details: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/4/too-much-tickets\nSource: D
 oTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/sfdanceworks-season-
 9-performance/
