BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Studio 8 Film Festival 2026: Where to? (Juror Night)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T213000
DTSTAMP:20261024T205625Z
UID:dothebay-17947955@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Studio 8 Film Festival presents:\nWhere to? (Juror Night)\n\nT
 his year's open call jurors show their own work: Nine Years Behind the Whe
 el (Ed Jones\, 1986)\, Lullaby To My Father and Lullaby To My Father: Redu
 x (Michael LaRocco\, 2019)\, and Lost or Found (Jacalyn White and Joell Ha
 llowell\, 2020).\n\nShot from the driver's seat of his night-shift cab\, E
 d Jones's Nine Years Behind the Wheel is a diary of San Francisco in the '
 80s and of an artist trying to keep going. Passengers\, SFAI openings\, No
  Nothing Cinema at 30 Berry Street\, a young Mike Henderson\, Marian Walla
 ce\, Michael Rudnick\, family\, friends\, bands: all of it filmed between 
 fares\, with wit and a great soundtrack.\n\nIn Lullaby To My Father and it
 s Redux\, Michael LaRocco revisits his father's absence after discovering 
 that his father had a second family in Vietnam during the war.\n\nLost or 
 Found gathers phone footage from friends and family across 21st-century Am
 erican life\, leading into the 2020 shelter-in-place\, and remixes it into
  improbable\, often funny juxtapositions.\n\nScreening will be followed by
  a conversation with all three jurors\, moderated by V. Vale of RE/Search.
 \n\nPoster artwork: Cristina Victor\n\nSF Artists Alumni presents:\n\nTick
 ets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbrite.com%2Fe
 %2Fstudio-8-film-festival-2026-juror-films-tickets-1999811326511%3Faff%3Do
 ddtdtcreator%26keep_tld%3Dtrue\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/
 11/6/studio-8-film-festival-juror-night-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35121429/ce18709b-9656-449e-b645-033fff1abb88.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261024T205625Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/6/studio-8-film-festival-juror-nig
 ht-tickets
END:VEVENT
