SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Culture & Diversity Film Festival presents:\n\nSHORT FILMS on 
 “MUSIC\, HARMONY & NATURE”\n\nDance Our Way to Heaven on Earth\n\nHawa
 iʻi born award-wining singer/songwriter\, Faith Rivera\, celebrates the j
 oy of self-expression and the power of community\, spreading love through 
 the universal languages of music and dance.\n\nGlidin’\n\nA lonely child
  dreams of being an astronaut\, achieves the dream with the help of a musi
 cian and finds not only a new world but a new home in the world once left 
 behind.\n\nRose & Leo\n\nIn the racially charged 1960s Florida\, a black h
 otel porter and a white performer defy societal norms to explore a forbidd
 en love. Based on the historic Supreme Court decision of McLaughin v. Flor
 ida\, this dramatic film gets at the heart of love\, hardship\, and inner 
 peace.\n\nElegy of Salt\n\nOn the shores of Utah’s Great Salt Lake\, a p
 hotographer with generations of family history on Antelope Island and a Sh
 oshone elder reflect on their relationships with a landscape facing an env
 ironmental crisis\, bringing silence\, music and nature in harmony.\n\nals
 o\n\nDOCUMENTARIES on “MYSTIC JOURNEYS”\n\nCommon Connections\n\nA lov
 e letter to the community that creates “The Common” at the Glastonbury
  music festival\, an area where the wildness of the rave meets the wisdom 
 of ancient spirituality\, creating magical dreams for the future.\n\nVagab
 ond in Red: Iquitos\n\nA filmmaker from Pittsburgh sets off across Peru on
  a personal healing journey\, exploring the landscape\, the people\, and a
 yahuasca. Poetic narra...\n\nTickets: https://filmfreeway.com/CultureDiver
 sityFilmFestival/tickets\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/10/
 culture-diversity-film-festival-films-on-music-harmony-nature-and-mystic-j
 ourneys-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
