DESCRIPTION:Basement VHS presents:\n\nIT (1990) ON VHS\n\nThe Master of Ho
 rror unleashes everything you were ever afraid of.\n\nIn 1960\, seven outc
 ast kids known as “The Losers’ Club” fight against an ancient shape-
 shifting alien who poses as a child-killing clown\, while also dealing wit
 h bullies and abusive parents. Thirty years later\, they reunite to stop t
 he creature once and for all when it returns to their hometown. The two-pa
 rt TV miniseries comes to the big screen courtesy of Basement VHS.\n\nIn-p
 erson Q&A with Director Tommy Lee Wallace to follow the screening.\n\nThis
  event has been postponed from its previously scheduled date on October 30
 th. All tickets for the original date are still valid and ticket-holders h
 ave been sent communications regarding refunds if necessary. If you did no
 t receive communication and cannot attend the new date\, please contact us
  before November 14th to receive a refund.\n\nBasement is an art collectiv
 e and VHS archive in the Mission District of San Francisco\, CA. They host
  a weekly film screening and radio show on Radio Valencia.\n\nTickets: htt
 ps://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/20263?siteToken=d2atbcege5knqsavn
 tt91g1250\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/it-on-vhs-ticke
