DESCRIPTION:Stand-Up Comedy at the Balboa Theatre\n\nA Packed Lineup of sh
 orter sets for up and coming Bay Area comedians during the first half of t
 he show\, with an intermission to grab another beer or popcorn from the lo
 bby or that right on time bathroom break. The second half of the show feat
 ures national touring and veteran comediansWith surprise pop-in guest sets
 .\n\nA night of laughs in the Richmond District you will not want to miss!
 \n\nHeadliner Johana Coca\n\nJohana Coca is a Los Angeles–based stand-up
  comedian with Honduran roots\, raised in Portland\, Oregon. She is a regu
 lar at the Laugh Factory Hollywood\, has opened for Iliza Shlesinger and G
 ary Owen\, and was featured on Season 2 of Iliza’s Locals\, now streamin
 g on Amazon Prime Video. She also won the Bend Comedy Festival joke compet
 ition. She is one of 14 children\, so she is desperate for your love and a
 ttention. Rooted in family\, culture\, and lived experience\, Johana turns
  personal stories into instantly relatable comedy. Her warmth and timing m
 ake every set feel like a conversation you don’t want to end with the co
 olest cousin you wish you had.\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.
 com/purchase/20219?siteToken=52wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\nDetails: https://
 dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/comedy-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
