BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LIVE MUSIC: June McDoom
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T220000
DTSTAMP:20261014T214646Z
UID:dothebay-17696032@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Throwin’ Bo’s presents:\n\nJune McDoom\n\nThere is a hush 
 most of us only knew as children\, the warm drift between familiar househo
 ld sounds and being carried to bed\, a place that belongs to you and to so
 me self you have not met yet. June McDoom's debut full-length\, Follow the
  Light\, lives in that dream space and then keeps walking\, slipping out o
 f time and waking somewhere new\, barely familiar enough to feel like home
  yet wholly your own.\n\nShe came up in a Jamaican household on the edge o
 f the Florida Everglades\, an existence built of extended family\, communa
 l care\, bass and harmonics. Her father\, a carpenter and a student of sou
 nd\, built his own speakers and kept three sound systems going across as m
 any rooms. His low end would rise through her bedroom floor like some wayw
 ard cat while she lay above it with folk records\, finding harmonies that 
 were new and hers alone. Two musics in one room. Lushness as past and prem
 onition.\n\nShe found folk on her own\, somewhere between the cast recordi
 ng of The Sound of Music and Simon and Garfunkel\, while everyone around h
 er called it sleepy music. She did not mind being the only one. The solitu
 de let her fall for harmony first\, before words\, before anything else\, 
 and harmony is still the thing she reaches for.\n\nGenerationally speaking
 \, the music was already in the air. Her grandfather\, Colin Smith\, is a 
 distinguished mento man who played banjo and guitar and built his own rumb
 a boxes\, worked to keep Jamaica's oldest acoustic folk form alive....\n\n
 Tickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbrite.com
 %2Fe%2F1996177913876%3Faff%3Doddtdtcreator\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/
 events/2026/12/12/live-music-june-mcdoom-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33726444/3995ced8-f5b8-4b9c-a535-6b0f822402a2.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T214646Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/12/live-music-june-mcdoom-tickets
END:VEVENT
